Seven Kingdoms: Modified (orchardroot/7kaa)
-----------------------------------
An actively developed mod fork of Seven Kingdoms: Ancient Adversaries,
based on release 2.15.6 (upstream: the3dfxdude/7kaa). New features land
on the `mod-base` branch; each larger feature is developed on a
`feature/*` branch and merged in.

Features so far
---------
* Turret -- a new defensive building (300 gold, 150 HP, hotkey U in the
  build menu, buildable by every civilization from the start). It fires
  arrows automatically at hostile units within 8 tiles: slowly when
  unmanned, faster as up to 4 soldiers are garrisoned (ranged soldiers
  count double). Implemented by completing the engine's stubbed
  firm-fired-projectile path. Reuses the Fort's graphics for now.
* Cheats menu -- a "Cheats" entry on the in-game menu (F10, hotkey C,
  single-player only) with the classic cheat effects: gold, food, all
  technology and gods, reveal map, town population, repairs, combat
  levels, immortal king and fast build. No more magic keystring, though
  it still works. Using any cheat still marks the score "(Cheated)".
* Rebuilt in-game menu -- the F10 menu is now drawn with real widget
  buttons instead of a baked bitmap: press animations, reliable
  hit-testing, translatable labels, and "Quit to OS" instead of
  "Quit to Windows".

Compatibility
---------
Save games use version 213: saves from the unmodified game are refused
(and vice versa), because the new building type changes the save layout.
Multiplayer with vanilla clients is not compatible.

Developing
---------
Build (macOS): ./configure CXXFLAGS="-std=gnu++11 -O2" && make -j6
Run from the source tree: SKDATA=data src/7kaa
Quick boot test: tools/smoke.sh

Game data lives in RES/SET archives under data/RESOURCE; the perl tools
in tools/ (deresx/libresx, dbfdump/libdb, dbf.pm) unpack and repack
them. Scripted, replayable data transforms document every change:
* tools/add_turret_data.pl -- the Turret's FIRM/FBUILD records and icon
* tools/make_turret_icon.py -- repaints the Fort icon's label to TURRET
* tools/patch_gamemenu_os.py -- "Quit to OS" on the old menu bitmap
  (kept for reference; the rebuilt menu no longer uses the bitmap)

Note: many source files are ISO-8859 encoded -- use `grep -a`, and keep
that encoding when editing.

Ideas / roadmap
---------
* Teach the AI to build and garrison turrets
* Dedicated turret artwork and encyclopedia entry
* More menu quality-of-life (the main menu is still bitmap-based)

